{
  "$comment": "#EDE-65 lane M (docs/round-9-contract.md §19): Embed, a nested genUI surface drawn in place, SANDBOXED. HAND-AUTHORED; replayed by src/embed.test.ts (the TS reference src/embed.ts), packages/exponential-ui-react/src/embed.test.tsx, packages/exponential-ui-solid/src/embed.test.tsx, apps/desktop/crates/eui-core/tests/embed_fixture.rs (eui_core::embed), apps/desktop/crates/eui-gpui/tests/embed.rs, the SwiftUI EmbedTests and the Compose EmbedTest. `surface` is a DATA prop: a binding `{\"@path\"}` AT THE TOP resolves against the host (the Embed's scope), nothing inside it ever does. `errorRoot` = what a bad surface paints instead (an error Alert titled `$string.embedInvalid`), the host around it unchanged. `parse`: the resolved `surface` value → `valid` and, when valid, the card's `data` (missing or null = {}); a card is an object with a sound `root` (string non-empty `id` + `component`; `props`, `on`, `style` objects when present; `children` an array of sound nodes; `slots` an object of sound nodes), `data` absent, null or an object, `version` absent or \"1.0\"; an unknown component inside a sound root is valid (the nested surface paints its Unknown placeholder). `render`: mount the host `root` with `data` under the neutral theme: every `texts` entry is painted (in order of the host's pre-order with the nested surface in place of its Embed), no `absent` entry is. `events`: mount, then press the inner node `press.node` of the `press.embed`-th painted Embed (0-based, painted order): the host hears exactly `actions` ({name, context}: the Embed's own `on.action` event with the payload {name: inner event name, context: inner event context} merged over the author's context, like any component payload; no `on.action` = nothing), its host-function handler hears `functions` (an inner host function is DENIED: never forwarded, its action stops), and afterwards every `texts` entry is painted and no `absent` one (an inner `set` writes the nested model only).",
